<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Delmatae</h1><p class="st-meta">180 BCE – 9 CE (approx.) · capital Delminium</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Illyrian people of the Dalmatian hinterland who fought Rome for two centuries and gave their name to the province of Dalmatia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Delmatae lived in the karst uplands behind the Adriatic coast, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delminium">Delminium</a> (near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomislavgrad">Tomislavgrad</a>). Around 180 BCE they broke away from the Illyrian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gentius">Gentius</a> and built their own league, extending their power over neighbouring peoples and the coastal towns.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their league joined communities of herders and farmers living in hillforts. They raided the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/daorsi">Daorsi</a> and the Greek cities of Issa's mainland colonies. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> fought them in 156–155 BCE, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/publius-cornelius-scipio-nasica-corculum">Scipio Nasica</a> destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delminium">Delminium</a>, and again in 119 and 78–76 BCE. In the winter of 48–47 BCE they defeated a Roman army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aulus-gabinius">Aulus Gabinius</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Octavian's campaign of 34–33 BCE took their strongholds such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/promona">Promona</a>. They rose again in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-illyrian-revolt">Great Illyrian Revolt</a> of 6–9 CE, and their last fortress, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andetrium">Andetrium</a>, fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> in 9 CE. Their name lived on in the Roman province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 180 BCE – 9 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:56.12%;width:3.76%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>180 BCE – 9 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Delminium</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Illyrian polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Illyrian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/croatia">Croatia</a>, <a href="/countries/bosnia-and-herzegovina">Bosnia and Herzegovina</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dalmatae</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-86&amp;focus=delmatae" aria-label="Delmatae on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5096 631 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Delmatae lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5416 887L5474 936M5416 887L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5474 936h0M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5416 887h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5416 887h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Delminium. <a href="/atlas?year=-86&amp;focus=delmatae">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
